WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.900
- To me, walking upside down on all fours

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.460
is as easy as walking on two feet.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.293
It's not scary or frightening
to me in the least.

00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:08.628
I've always been flexible.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.713
But not just a little bit
flexible, I'm really flexible.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.260
Little did I know that
this ability was, in fact,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.063
the talent that would
change my life completely.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.020
I'm Troy James, and I'm a creature actor.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.320
I play creatures on TV and movies

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.873
that move in ways that
make the audience squirm.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.970
My talent is that all of my joints-

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:46.340
my legs, my arms, my
shoulders, my fingers-

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.513
they just bend however I want them to.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.200
So if you need an alien, a
demon, or a nonhuman creature

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.650
that doesn't move in the ways
that normal human people do,

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.600
that's when you call me.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.960
It looks like what I do
is extremely painful.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:04.573
Really, it doesn't hurt at all.

00:01:07.972 --> 00:01:10.880
I don't know why I am as flexible as I am.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.970
It's just something I was born with.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.040
I'm the only one in my family

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.293
who can bend his arms
and legs the way I do.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.090
I didn't think it was that strange

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:22.030
until other kids told me it was,

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.740
but they weren't very nice about it.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.270
And I remember being very
embarrassed and I hid it away

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:29.260
because what makes you
different when you're growing up

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:31.040
isn't something to be proud of.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.423
I hid it for a long time.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.640
But that all changed when I got a job

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.120
as an amusement park ride operator.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.950
It was a hot day,

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.980
the ride was down for
some reason or another,

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:45.230
the guests were getting kind of ornery,

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:48.570
and I thought, why don't
I show them what I can do?

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.670
And I went up and down the line

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:54.870
making really cool shapes with
my body, and it was a hit.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.830
And that was the first time

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:00.050
I'd gotten that sort of positive
reaction from other people,

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.213
showcasing my talent.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:04.220
I never thought my ability

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.350
was anything more than a
really cool party trick.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:09.657
My friend put his camera
up to me and said,

00:02:09.657 --> 00:02:11.520
"Show me something cool."

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.720
Then he posted it on the internet,

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.820
and all of a sudden, my
phone started ringing.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:19.050
I started getting calls
to be cast in TV shows,

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.363
and I didn't look back.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:25.610
If you had told me a year ago,
I was going to be an actor,

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.790
I would've laughed at you.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.730
But after some of my performances,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.650
people have told me that
it's not just the way

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.490
I move my body that's effective,
it's the acting behind it.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.750
I bring a reaction to the audience.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.210
I can thrill them, so to speak.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:41.820
Coming from a place
where you were ostracized

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:45.103
as I was as a child, I can
bring that out as a creature.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:50.260
It's interesting that something
that I hid for so long

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:55.260
is now taking me places that
I never imagined I would go.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.160
I believe everyone has a super power.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.500
And you may not know it's a super power,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.800
but if it's something

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.980
that you're passionate
about that makes you happy,

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.370
I think sharing it with the world

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.220
may not be such a bad idea after all.

